%<HELP>	#.($548)Configure|Windows|Source|Image Width
%<HELP>	#The \bImage^Width\r command allows you to adjust the width of the field
%<HELP>	#used for the hexadecimal image of the disassembled instruction in the
%<HELP>	#Source Window when the display mode is Code or Mixed.  Note that this
%<HELP>	#setting does \unot\r apply in the \l($113)Display/Alter|Asm/Dasm\m Menu
%<HELP>	#(Disassembler & Single-Line Assembler).
%<HELP>	#There, the maximum possible field width is always used.
%<HELP>	#.sp 1
%<HELP>	#Hint:^^You can use this command to effectively increase the space
%<HELP>	#(width) available for the \l($533)Annotated^Source\m information in the
%<HELP>	#Source Window if that Annotated Source information overwrites part of
%<HELP>	#the operand field of a disassembled instruction.
%<HELP&A25>	#.($549)Goto | Register File Window
%<HELP&A25>	#When you are browsing/perusing the Register File window,
%<HELP&A25>	#you can examine and/or change Byte, Word or Dword register
%<HELP&A25>	#values as described
%<HELP&A25>	#in the \l($61)Configure|Windows|Goto\m command.
%<HELP>	#.($551)Catalog of iceMASTER MCS251 Products
%<HELP>	#.sp 1
%<HELP>	#.in +3 {
%<HELP>	#.ti -3
%<HELP>	#\b%rs1-MCS251 Modular Emulator\r:
%<HELP>	#.sp 1
%<HELP>	#The %rs2 \b%rs1-MCS251 Modular\r emulator supports the
%<HELP>	#Intel MCS251 family of devices.
%<HELP>	#The \b%rs1-MCS251 Modular\r emulator consists of a small
%<HELP>	#emulator base unit,
%<HELP>	#attached to a small probe card (pod) via an umbilical cable.
%<HELP>	#The probe card, which contains the device being emulated,
%<HELP>	#inserts into the socket for the device in your target
%<HELP>	#development system.  Probe cards are available supporting the entire
%<HELP>	#Intel MCS251 family.
%<HELP>	#The emulator base unit connects to the
%<HELP>	#host PC (personal computer) via either a standard bi-directional
%<HELP>	#parallel port, or a standard RS-232-C serial
%<HELP>	#communications link operating at 57.6K baud.
%<HELP>	#.sp 1
%<HELP>	#The \b%rs1-MCS251 Modular\r emulator is an advanced,
%<HELP>	#high-performance, full-featured, economical,
%<HELP>	#small profile/footprint emulator supporting
%<HELP>	#full probe card interchangeability within the Intel MCS251 family.
%<HELP>	#.in -3 }
%<HELP>	#.sp 2
